USC: don't combine byte or word loads into fetches

On SGX543 an LDAB or LDAW with the FETCH flag writes only its first
destination, so four char loads combined into one fetch returned one byte
and left the rest unset.  The IMG compiler never makes such a fetch.  Only
combine dword loads.

diff --git a/tools/intern/usc2/reorder.c b/tools/intern/usc2/reorder.c
index b35a78b..250dadd 100644
--- a/tools/intern/usc2/reorder.c
+++ b/tools/intern/usc2/reorder.c
@@ -244,6 +244,15 @@ IMG_VOID BuildFetchInstructions(PINTERMEDIATE_STATE psState)
 
 		uPrimSize = psBaseInst->u.psLoadMemConst->uDataSize;
 
+		/*
+			A byte or word load with FETCH on SGX543 writes only its first
+			destination (tested on hardware; the IMG compiler never makes one).
+		*/
+		if (uPrimSize < LONG_SIZE)
+		{
+			continue;
+		}
+
 		uLastStaticOffset = GetFetchStaticOffset(psBaseInst);
 
 		uFetchCount = 1;
